WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:04.145
Poly(lactic acid) may keep its familiar bulk chemistry

00:00:04.145 --> 00:00:07.740
while the interface that meets its environment changes.

00:00:11.717 --> 00:00:16.500
Cold plasma can activate a polymer surface, opening opportunities

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:21.283
for grafting chemistry without replacing the entire underlying material.

00:00:26.217 --> 00:00:32.119
Our coauthored research examined grafting approaches involving fumaric and ascorbic

00:00:32.119 --> 00:00:38.021
acids on PLA films, connecting surface chemistry to material characterisation.

00:00:43.883 --> 00:00:48.703
Morphology and chemical characterisation can tell whether a

00:00:48.703 --> 00:00:53.523
proposed surface transformation is consistent with observed material properties.

00:00:58.467 --> 00:01:03.060
The biologically relevant encounter happens at an interface. A

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:07.653
changed surface does not itself establish performance inside a patient.

00:01:12.383 --> 00:01:16.353
This study illustrates how targeted chemistry can change

00:01:16.353 --> 00:01:20.322
the questions a biodegradable polymer is able to answer.
